fzf-pinyin is a modified distribution of fzf, maintained independently at
https://github.com/zhiyozhao/fzf-pinyin. Its executable is named fzfp.

The original fzf is Copyright (c) 2013-2026 Junegunn Choi and is licensed
under the MIT License. The complete original copyright and permission
notice is retained in LICENSE. Upstream source and history are preserved;
README.fzf.md is the original README at the pinned upstream commit.

The modifications add Mandarin pinyin matching, source-coordinate scoring
and highlighting, prefix-safe candidate caching, documentation, tests and
fzfp packaging. Pinyin extensions are Copyright (c) 2026 fzf-pinyin contributors
and are also licensed under MIT.

Pronunciation data and code from go-pinyin/pinyin-data retain their MIT
notices. Additional dependency notices and complete license texts are listed
in THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md and docs/licenses/.
